--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -7,6 +7,19 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- **Dolt CPU runaway watchdog (`GC_DOLT_CPU_WATCHDOG`).** A goroutine spawned
+  alongside the managed `dolt sql-server` samples its CPU every 15 s via `ps`.
+  If usage exceeds 200 % for ≥ 60 s (4 consecutive samples) it emits a
+  structured `severity=critical` alert to the supervisor log, sends SIGKILL to
+  the dolt process, and lets the existing supervisor restart path recover the
+  server. A single-burst spike (e.g. a large `DOLT_MERGE`) does not trigger a
+  kill; only sustained pathological spin loops do. Disable with
+  `GC_DOLT_CPU_WATCHDOG=0`; override the sample interval in tests with
+  `GC_DOLT_CPU_WATCHDOG_INTERVAL_MS`. Defense-in-depth for the 2026-06-16
+  incident where a `DOLT_CLONE` against a git URL consumed 1000 % CPU.
+
 ### Changed
 
 - **Version pins on builtin packs are honored: the binary only pre-seeds
